                    # The buggy code uses start() function in cli.py, but here we test Chain class directly

                    # Instead, we call chain._run_loop() if exists, else simulate the steps from start()

                    # The Chain class does not expose _run_loop, so we simulate by calling chain.__call__ or chain.start() if any

                    # The Chain class does not have a public run method, so we call the internal method that triggers the loop
